# Execution Plan System

Spec: PlanSystem
Purpose:
  Define the Execution Plan object — generated from an Intent after
  requirement extraction, knowledge resolution, and architecture constraints.
  A plan is NOT a task list; it is a dependency graph with execution modes,
  approval gates, risk levels, and adaptive replanning capabilities.

Owns: plans/

## Execution Plan Schema

  @plan.P12

  goal:
      @intent.I44

  tasks:
      T100  Domain model
      T101  Repository
      T102  Provider integration
      T103  Refund service
      T104  API
      T105  Tests
      T106  Review

  edges:
      T100 -> T103
      T101 -> T103
      T102 -> T103
      T103 -> T104
      T103 -> T105
      T104 -> T106
      T105 -> T106

  parallel:
      T100
      T101
      T102

  critical_path:
      T100 -> T103 -> T104 -> T106

  risk:
      HIGH

  status:
      ACTIVE

## Execution Modes

  AUTO      — execute plan autonomously per policy
  ASSISTED  — execute with human checkpoints
  STEP      — pause after each task; human says "continue"
  DRY_RUN   — simulate without any code changes
  REVIEW    — human reviews plan before execution

## Approval Gates

  Special nodes in the execution graph:

  @approval.architecture  — architectural changes require approval
  @approval.security      — security-sensitive changes require approval
  @approval.production     — production changes require approval
  @approval.migration      — data/schema migrations require approval
  @approval.release        — releases require approval

  AI prepares evidence (change, why, impact, risk, tests, decision)
  for human review at each gate.

## Plan Versioning

  Plans are versioned with semantic versioning:
    @plan.P12 v1
    @plan.P12 v2
    @plan.P12 v3

  MAJOR → architecture/constraint change
  MINOR → added/removed tasks
  PATCH → correction/improvement

## Plan Revision Reason

  Every revision MUST include:
    changed:
        added T102b
    reason:
        provider requires webhook confirmation
    evidence:
        @reference.R91
    impact:
        medium

## Adaptive Planning

  Plans are NOT immutable. When new evidence is discovered:

  1. PAUSE current execution
  2. REPLAN with new evidence
  3. VALIDATE new plan (circular deps, missing skills, etc.)
  4. RESUME from last checkpoint

  All plan changes are observable:
    PLAN_CHANGED event emitted
    No silent replanning

## Circular Dependency Detection

  System MUST detect cycles before execution:
    T100 → T101 → T102 → T100
    → CYCLE_DETECTED → plan blocked

## Missing Dependency Detection

  If task requires @skill that doesn't exist:
    → missing skill detected
    → BLOCKED
    → AI may insert research task: T110 Research idempotency pattern

## Execution Event Stream

  PLAN_CREATED
  TASK_READY
  TASK_CLAIMED
  TASK_STARTED
  DISCOVERY_FOUND
  PLAN_CHANGED
  TASK_BLOCKED
  TASK_COMPLETED
  PROOF_CREATED
  REVIEW_STARTED
  REVIEW_FAILED
  REVIEW_PASSED
  PLAN_COMPLETED

## Rules

  [PLAN-01] Plan ≠ Task list. Plan is a dependency graph.
  [PLAN-02] Plan ≠ Workflow. Workflow is the standard process; plan is project-specific execution graph.
  [PLAN-03] Plan ≠ Skill. Skill is how; plan is which tasks and order.
  [PLAN-04] Plan MUST be versioned. Every change creates a new revision.
  [PLAN-05] Plan changes MUST NOT be silent. Emit PLAN_CHANGED event.
  [PLAN-06] Critical changes MUST require approval gate.
  [PLAN-07] Circular dependencies MUST be detected before execution.
  [PLAN-08] Missing skills/dependencies MUST block plan execution.
  [PLAN-09] Execution MUST emit event stream for knowledge extraction.
  [PLAN-10] Plan MUST track critical path for bottleneck identification.

